container.sim.traits1=Brave
container.sim.traits2=Brave folk make much better soldiers. They wait half the time between killing a mob that an ordinary soldier of that level would. Their soldier skill also levels up twice as fast.
container.sim.traits3=Dwarven Heritage
container.sim.traits4=Folk with a dwarven heritage are faster at diggy diggy hole. Give one a pickaxe and they will excavate twice as fast as an ordinary miner. While they prefer mining, they still make good, fast glass makers.
container.sim.traits5=Friendly
container.sim.traits6=Friendly folk are always out to make friends. They will rarely have poor relationships with other folk and become unhappy when they have no friends.
container.sim.traits7=Green Thumb
container.sim.traits8=Folk with a green thumb make much better crop farmers. They can plant, plough and harvest twice as fast, meaning you make twice the amount of produce.
container.sim.traits9=Hates the Outdoors
container.sim.traits10=Folk that hate the outdoors tend to warp more frequently They dislike open spaces, and hate working on farms.
container.sim.traits11=Loves the Outdoors
container.sim.traits12=Folk that love the outdoors love taking leisurely strolls. They love open spaces, and working outside will make their day.
container.sim.traits13=Night Owl
container.sim.traits14=Night Owl folk won't spend much time indoors upon nightfall. They will wander during the night. Night Owl folk will continue terraforming and building work throughout the night.
container.sim.traits15=Religious
container.sim.traits16=Religious folk like to visit church daily to pray. Being unable to do so makes them unhappy. Make sure you build a church in your town.
container.sim.traits17=Church
container.sim.traits18=Attending Church
container.sim.traits19=Strong
container.sim.traits20=Strong folk can perform manual labour faster. Be it mining, cutting wood, building or digging sand.
container.sim.traits21=Workaholic
container.sim.traits22=Workaholic folk enjoy working, and will develop skills twice as fast as an ordinary folk. Unemployment makes these folk unhappy. Keep those employment rates up!
